{"body":"Closes #73\n\n**ENVIRONMENT_BLOCKED — P1_SMOKE_CAPTURE_GUARD_ERROR.** The first observed Stage-1 failure was the executor capture guard rejecting permitted local bond copper and throwing before raw Circuit JSON was saved. This is an executor verification/capture procedure failure, not evidence of EDA/backend incapability.\n\nThe subsequent converter invocation was an additional operation **after that first failure**, contrary to immediate-stop discipline. It observed the secondary environment obstacle **P1_CONVERTER_MODULE_LOAD / ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND** (the selected scripts-disabled kicadts deployment lacked dist/index.js). That obstacle is not the first terminal gate. **immediate_stop_compliance = false** and the sequence deviation remain explicit.\n\nThis records-only correction addresses the PMO finding on reviewed HEAD 137f2e5e5cf267177899b06ca824f2daa29153dc. Report, attempt/failure/effort records, README, docs/project-status and Dashboard now agree on the failure order. Ambiguous qualification_execution_complete was replaced by **terminal_reporting_complete = true** and **technical_qualification_complete = false**. No PMO acceptance of this correction is claimed.\n\nHistorical execution: checkout/hash checks, isolated setup and headless help/binding inspection; one synthetic frontend render followed by one failed converter module-load invocation. Two Freerouting invocations were help-only. Main initial/confirmation **0/0**, smoke routing **0**. No new experimental process was launched in this correction.\n\nStage 1 remains partial. Stage 2–4, usable smoke roundtrip, Main generation/transfer, exact USB_SHELL_BOND bridge, source/geometry/semantic maps, meaningful ERC, source/schematic/PCB parity, DSN/SES, routing/DRC, independent copper reconciliation/geometry fault tests and reproducibility remain **NOT ENTERED**. Main acceptance metrics remain **null** and evidence completeness **PARTIAL**. Missing raw JSON and unknown individual numeric exits/timestamps were not reconstructed, inferred or fabricated. The recorded secondary log mtime is not the first exception timestamp.\n\nValidation: updated artifact/run-contract hashes; **16 adversarial reporting cases**, including secondary-as-first misclassification across all records, reversed observations, hidden post-failure operation, false immediate stop, false technical completion and guessed exit code. **369 protected original files**, five fixed baseline hashes and production **tscircuit 0.0.2646** preserved. **31 non-editable qualification files**, including original raw logs, package archives and executed scripts, are byte-identical to the reviewed HEAD. Record-only diff whitelist, local references/docs/Dashboard agreement, node --check and git diff --check passed. Reporting PASS is not geometry/backend qualification PASS.\n\nTool pins/install records are unchanged: frontend 0.0.2748 / core 0.0.2097 / props 0.0.689 / circuit-json 0.0.516, Bun 1.2.22; converter 0.0.230; kicadts f3ea106bdc65ca901e9b23255ad3be0bd2a624ab; KiCad 9.0.9; Freerouting 2.5.0; Microsoft Java 25.0.4.1; Node 24.21.0/npm 11.19.0; Python 3.12.3 / orchestration 3.14.2. Historical effort estimates remain estimates; measured engineer-hours, human effort and complete unattended elapsed time are unobserved. The effort record now acknowledges the post-first-failure converter operation.\n\nNo reinstall, build, dependency substitution, smoke/converter rerun, DSN/SES, Main generation, routing or ERC/DRC experiment occurred in this correction. No candidate change, production dependency change, historical design/evidence/decision change, adoption, exception, Human Gate, merge or auto-merge is authorized.\n\nUSB NPTH OPEN — PRE-ORDER DFM REVIEW REQUIRED. Backend adoption and candidate switching remain unapproved. Reusable artifacts are limited to recorded setup/help observations and preserved packages/logs; no board, route, semantic map or physical verifier is qualified. Further work requires PO disposition